{% doc %}
  Ambient ground — the page's moving backdrop, promoted from
  sv-shop-by-age once the owner asked for it to run through the page.

  Three depths of gold thread and eight motes, each layer drifting on
  its own axis and tempo so they read as depth rather than one sheet
  sliding. Styles live in sv-system.css §08c; keyframes are transform
  only and §08's reduced-motion rule freezes the whole thing into a
  still engraving.

  Contract: the host section carries `sv-amb-host` on its [data-sv]
  root (positions it and clips the drift) and keeps its content inside
  `.w`, which §08c lifts above the layer. Render this as the first
  visual child:

      <section class="sv-age sv-amb-host" data-sv>
        {%- render 'sv-ambient' -%}
        <div class="w"> ... </div>
      </section>

  Purely decorative: aria-hidden, pointer-events none, never read by
  assistive tech.
{% enddoc %}

